# Flutter — GridView

## 1. What is `GridView`?

`GridView` displays widgets in a **grid layout**.

Instead of:

```text
Item 1
Item 2
Item 3
Item 4
```

you can have:

```text
┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐
│ Item 1  │  │ Item 2  │
└─────────┘  └─────────┘

┌─────────┐  ┌─────────┐
│ Item 3  │  │ Item 4  │
└─────────┘  └─────────┘
```

Common uses:

* Products
* Categories
* Photos
* Movies
* Food items
* Dashboard cards

---

# 2. Basic GridView

```dart
GridView.count(
  crossAxisCount: 2,

  children: [

    Card(
      child: Center(
        child: Text("Item 1"),
      ),
    ),

    Card(
      child: Center(
        child: Text("Item 2"),
      ),
    ),

    Card(
      child: Center(
        child: Text("Item 3"),
      ),
    ),

    Card(
      child: Center(
        child: Text("Item 4"),
      ),
    ),

  ],
)
```

### `crossAxisCount`

This controls the number of columns.

```dart
crossAxisCount: 2
```

means:

```text
Column 1    Column 2
   ↓           ↓
 Item 1      Item 2
 Item 3      Item 4
 Item 5      Item 6
```

---

# 3. Dynamic Grid — `GridView.builder`

Just like `ListView.builder`, use `GridView.builder` when your data is dynamic.

```dart
GridView.builder(
  itemCount: products.length,

  gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: 2,
  ),

  itemBuilder: (context, index) {

    final product = products[index];

    return Card(
      child: Center(
        child: Text(product["title"]!),
      ),
    );
  },
)
```

The important difference is:

```text
ListView.builder
        ↓
one item per row

GridView.builder
        ↓
multiple items per row
```

---

# 4. Dynamic Product Grid

Using the same type of data:

```dart
List<Map<String, String>> products = [
  {
    "image": "https://picsum.photos/id/1/300",
    "title": "Laptop",
    "info": "Powerful laptop",
  },
  {
    "image": "https://picsum.photos/id/2/300",
    "title": "Headphones",
    "info": "Wireless audio",
  },
  {
    "image": "https://picsum.photos/id/3/300",
    "title": "Phone",
    "info": "5G smartphone",
  },
  {
    "image": "https://picsum.photos/id/4/300",
    "title": "Watch",
    "info": "Fitness tracking",
  },
];
```

Then:

```dart
GridView.builder(
  padding: EdgeInsets.all(10),

  itemCount: products.length,

  gridDelegate: SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: 2,

    crossAxisSpacing: 10,

    mainAxisSpacing: 10,

    childAspectRatio: 0.75,
  ),

  itemBuilder: (context, index) {

    final product = products[index];

    return Card(
      child: Column(
        crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,

        children: [

          Expanded(
            child: Image.network(
              product["image"]!,
              width: double.infinity,
              fit: BoxFit.cover,
            ),
          ),

          Padding(
            padding: EdgeInsets.all(10),

            child: Column(
              crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,

              children: [

                Text(
                  product["title"]!,
                  style: TextStyle(
                    fontSize: 16,
                    fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                  ),
                ),

                SizedBox(height: 4),

                Text(
                  product["info"]!,
                  maxLines: 1,
                  overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis,
                ),

              ],
            ),
          ),
        ],
      ),
    );
  },
)
```

---

# 5. Important Grid Properties

### `crossAxisCount`

Number of columns.

```dart
crossAxisCount: 2
```

or:

```dart
crossAxisCount: 3
```

---

### `crossAxisSpacing`

Horizontal space between columns.

```dart
crossAxisSpacing: 10
```

---

### `mainAxisSpacing`

Vertical space between rows.

```dart
mainAxisSpacing: 10
```

---

### `childAspectRatio`

Controls the shape/size of each grid item.

```dart
childAspectRatio: 0.75
```

Lower value → taller item.

Higher value → wider/shorter item.

---

# 6. GridView vs ListView

| ListView                 | GridView                         |
| ------------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| Items arranged in rows   | Items arranged in columns + rows |
| Usually one item per row | Multiple items per row           |
| Contacts                 | Products                         |
| Messages                 | Categories                       |
| Songs                    | Photo gallery                    |

### Remember

```text
ListView
↓
1 column

GridView
↓
2+ columns
```

---

# 7. `GridView.count` vs `GridView.builder`

### `GridView.count`

Good when you have a small number of fixed widgets.

```dart
GridView.count(
  crossAxisCount: 2,
  children: [
    Text("A"),
    Text("B"),
    Text("C"),
    Text("D"),
  ],
)
```

### `GridView.builder`

Better for dynamic data.

```dart
GridView.builder(
  itemCount: products.length,

  gridDelegate:
      SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
    crossAxisCount: 2,
  ),

  itemBuilder: (context, index) {
    return Text(products[index]["title"]!);
  },
)
```

For real apps, **`GridView.builder` is the important one to remember**.

---

# 8. Important Warning

Just like `ListView`, a `GridView` needs a proper height when placed inside a `Column`.

Avoid:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Text("Products"),

    GridView.builder(
      itemCount: 20,
      // ...
    ),
  ],
)
```

Use:

```dart
Column(
  children: [

    Text("Products"),

    Expanded(
      child: GridView.builder(
        itemCount: 20,

        gridDelegate:
            SliverGridDelegateWithFixedCrossAxisCount(
          crossAxisCount: 2,
        ),

        itemBuilder: (context, index) {
          return Card(
            child: Text("Product $index"),
          );
        },
      ),
    ),
  ],
)
```

---

# 9. Mental Model

```text
GridView.builder
       ↓
  itemCount
       ↓
How many items?
       ↓
gridDelegate
       ↓
How should the grid be arranged?
       ↓
itemBuilder
       ↓
What should each item look like?
       ↓
index
       ↓
Which data should this item use?
```

---

## One-line revision

**`GridView` displays widgets in a scrollable grid, and `GridView.builder` is used to efficiently create dynamic grid items from data.**
